## Attribution

This part isn't a legal requirement — the MIT terms above already require the
copyright notice to travel with the software. This is just me asking.

If you use, modify, or build on LaLog, I'd be glad if you kept my name on it. A
line in your README or an "about" section — something like "based on LaLog by
lawaty, https://github.com/lawaty/lalog" — is more than enough.

And if you publish a fork, please leave the copyright line in place and say where
the original came from. You're free to change anything else you like.

Thanks. It means a lot.
